WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:04.340
C programs can use many IPC mechanisms.

2
00:00:04.440 --> 00:00:08.360
Pipes and named pipes can connect producers and consumers.

3
00:00:08.460 --> 00:00:12.700
Unix domain sockets and TCP sockets can carry structured requests.

4
00:00:12.800 --> 00:00:17.120
Shared memory can expose the same bytes to multiple processes.

5
00:00:17.220 --> 00:00:19.780
Message queues provide queued exchange.

6
00:00:19.880 --> 00:00:22.200
Signals communicate limited events.

7
00:00:22.300 --> 00:00:27.180
Platform-specific handles and descriptors can extend what one process can grant to another.

8
00:00:27.460 --> 00:00:31.300
These mechanisms are not interchangeable from a security perspective.

9
00:00:31.400 --> 00:00:42.200
They differ in naming, access control, peer identity support, message boundaries, buffering, reliability, cleanup behavior, and how naturally they fit the workflow.

10
00:00:42.300 --> 00:00:47.820
A secure design chooses the mechanism that matches the trust boundary and the operational requirement.

11
00:00:48.100 --> 00:00:52.660
Byte-stream channels are common, but they do not automatically preserve message boundaries.

12
00:00:52.760 --> 00:01:00.040
If a protocol sends structured messages over a stream, the receiver needs explicit framing, parsing, and validation.

13
00:01:00.140 --> 00:01:07.260
A single read may contain part of a message, one message, or parts of several messages depending on timing and buffering.

14
00:01:07.540 --> 00:01:10.100
Shared memory has a different shape.

15
00:01:10.200 --> 00:01:15.080
It can be efficient, but it gives multiple processes access to the same region.

16
00:01:15.180 --> 00:01:21.980
That means layout, versioning, initialization, synchronization, and permissions all become part of the contract.

17
00:01:22.080 --> 00:01:28.160
Shared memory should not be treated as a shortcut around authorization or input validation.

18
00:01:28.440 --> 00:01:32.520
Signal-based communication is limited and should be used carefully.

19
00:01:32.620 --> 00:01:38.380
Signals can be useful for simple notifications, but they are not a good place to carry complex trusted state.

20
00:01:38.480 --> 00:01:48.160
Across all IPC choices, the security design should start from the mechanism's real properties rather than from the assumption that local communication is safe by default.
